WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.078
Operational technology, usually shortened to OT, is the collection of hardware and software used to monitor or control physical processes.

00:00:09.078 --> 00:00:16.045
OT reads conditions in the real world, makes control decisions, and causes equipment to act.

00:00:16.045 --> 00:00:28.079
A temperature sensor, a controller that opens a valve, and the workstation that shows an operator the process state can all belong to the same OT environment.

00:00:28.079 --> 00:00:32.934
OT is present wherever digital systems interact with physical operations.

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:38.212
Manufacturing plants use it to run production lines and industrial robots.

00:00:38.212 --> 00:00:43.068
Electric utilities use it to monitor substations and balance power.

00:00:43.068 --> 00:00:47.501
Water facilities control pumps, treatment stages, and chemical dosing.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:50.668
Transportation systems manage signaling and traffic.

00:00:50.668 --> 00:00:55.946
Building automation controls heating, ventilation, access, lighting, and life-safety support systems.

00:00:55.946 --> 00:01:00.802
This physical connection distinguishes OT from a conventional information system.

00:01:00.802 --> 00:01:05.235
A business application primarily stores, processes, or communicates data.

00:01:05.235 --> 00:01:12.202
An OT system may do those things, but its purpose is to influence a process.

00:01:12.202 --> 00:01:17.480
Incorrect data in an office report can cause a business problem.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:24.447
An incorrect control value can stop machinery, damage equipment, release material, or create unsafe conditions.

00:01:24.447 --> 00:01:27.614
OT environments are therefore cyber-physical systems.

00:01:27.614 --> 00:01:34.158
Digital components, networks, software, operators, machinery, and the underlying process must be considered together.

00:01:34.158 --> 00:01:41.125
Security cannot be evaluated solely by looking at an operating system version or firewall rule.

00:01:41.125 --> 00:01:52.314
Analysts must understand what the system controls, how operators use it, what safe operation requires, and what happens when communications or control functions are disrupted.

00:01:52.314 --> 00:01:56.748
OT security protects the dependable operation of these systems.

00:01:56.748 --> 00:02:04.559
That includes preventing unauthorized changes, detecting abnormal behavior, preserving reliable visibility for operators, and supporting safe recovery.

00:02:04.559 --> 00:02:09.415
The central question is not only, “Is the data protected?

00:02:09.415 --> 00:02:15.537
” It is also, “Can the physical operation continue safely and as intended?

00:02:15.537 --> 00:02:16.593
”
